# skeepto — Sk file naming

When **creating a new file** under `skeepto/src/`, the basename must start with **`Sk`** (PascalCase after `Sk`). `Skeepto…` is also allowed (it starts with `Sk`).

## Required

```text
✅ src/spreadsheet/SkRangeToHtmlTable.js
✅ src/component/SkMyDialog.js
✅ src/SkeeptoLang.js
```

## Imports

Import paths must match the real filename (case-sensitive):

```javascript
import { foo } from './SkJsonViewFormatHydrate.js';
// not './jsonViewFormatHydrate.js'
```

## Exceptions (do not rename; no Sk prefix required)

- Static assets: `*.css`, `*.svg`, `*.webp`, `*.png`, `*.json` (data), fonts
- CRA/bootstrap entry points already in the tree: `index.js`, `App.js`, `App.css`
- Test/setup files under `src/setupTests.js`, `src/reportWebVitals.js`
- Files outside `skeepto/src/` (e.g. `Node/Server/`, `public/`, config at repo root)

When adding a module next to existing non-`Sk` legacy files, prefer **`Sk…`** for the **new** file rather than extending the old naming pattern.
